From: Aadharsh Pannirselvam <aadharsh@archetype.fund>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 16:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] decoder: deblock behind reconstruction

AVM deblocks after the last tile is decoded, so on a frame whose tiles
finish unevenly the filter waits for the slowest one. av2/decoder/
lf_pipeline.c runs the same filter (AVM's own vert/horz functions) as
per-row, per-plane tasks on Grand Central Dispatch: V(r) once rows r and
r+1 are reconstructed in every tile column, H(r) after V(r-1) and V(r).

Every photo in the corpus allows global IntraBC, which predicts from
unfiltered pixels anywhere above. A task copies each finished row of each
tile column into an unfiltered shadow; V(r) waits for row r's copies, and
IntraBC reads that start above row r-1 go to the shadow (IbcShadow in
blockd.h, decided in dec_calc_subpel_params_and_extend and the morph
template). Rows r-1 and r stay on the frame: nothing filters them while
row r decodes.

Inter frames, row-MT and single-threaded decodes keep the usual pass;
AVM_LF_PIPELINE=0 turns it off. 25 of 25 bit-exact; 2,000+ decodes at
2-14 threads hash identically. Two controls fail as they should: reading
the frame instead of the shadow changes 3 files, and dropping V(r)'s wait
on row r+1 makes decodes differ run to run.
